  "label": "Camel as Symbol of the Middle East",
  "description": "Camels are culturally and geographically associated with the Middle East and North Africa, often used as a visual shorthand to represent people or cultures from those regions. This association is not inherently negative but is exploited in memes like this one to link the camels (and by extension, Middle Easterners) with negative stereotypes.",
